# What an agent presents to the k3s server to join the cluster.
#
# The server draws it once at first start and keeps it; it is read rather than chosen:
#
#   ssh vmk3s sudo cat /var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/node-token
#
# The whole `K10<hash>::server:<password>` string, hash included. The hash pins the cluster CA,
# so an agent handed the password alone joins nothing.
#
# Changing this on the server is not a rotation. The server's bootstrap data is encrypted with
# it, and a server restarted under a different one no longer reads its own cluster.
k3s-agent-token: K10PLACEHOLDER::server:PLACEHOLDER
